  evidence table at the end of this document.

Exit gate: the checked-in baseline identifies every suite and assertion surface,
and reproduces exactly the accepted 328-pass/four-failure state.

Phase 0 recorded evidence (2026-07-18):

- Commands ran in fresh `pwsh -NoProfile` child processes. The inherited Codex
  process PATH did not include the installed Lua toolchain, so each successful
  clean-process probe explicitly prepended
  `C:\Users\Sisco\AppData\Local\Programs\Lua\bin`. A raw `pwsh -NoProfile`
  invocation without that prerequisite failed before discovery with
  `LuaRocks was not found on PATH.` This is recorded environment setup, not a
  test-suite failure.
- The principal baseline commands were:

```powershell
pwsh -NoProfile -Command "& {
    `$env:PATH = 'C:\Users\Sisco\AppData\Local\Programs\Lua\bin;' + `$env:PATH
    & '.\Tools\Run-UnitTests.ps1'
}"

pwsh -NoProfile -Command "& {
    `$env:PATH = 'C:\Users\Sisco\AppData\Local\Programs\Lua\bin;' + `$env:PATH
    & '.\Tools\Run-UnitTests.ps1' -v `
        'Test_attributes_test.test attributes: physical above race median'
}"

pwsh -NoProfile -Command "& {
    `$env:PATH = 'C:\Users\Sisco\AppData\Local\Programs\Lua\bin;' + `$env:PATH
    `$env:LUAUNIT_SMOKE_FORCE_FAILURE = '1'
    & '.\Tools\Run-UnitTests.ps1' -v `
        'Test_luaunit_setup_test.test_opt_in_failure_path'
}"

pwsh -NoProfile -Command "& {
    `$env:PATH = 'C:\Users\Sisco\AppData\Local\Programs\Lua\bin;' + `$env:PATH
    & '.\Tools\Build.ps1' -LiveReload:`$false
}"

pwsh -NoProfile -Command "& {
    `$env:PATH = 'C:\Users\Sisco\AppData\Local\Programs\Lua\bin;' + `$env:PATH
    & '.\Tests\package_tools_test.ps1'
}"
```

- The full test command ran 332 tests in 57 discovered files: 328 succeeded and
  exactly four failed. LuaUnit returned code 4; the PowerShell runner restored
  its process environment, threw `LuaUnit tests failed with exit code 4.`, and
  the child process returned 1.
- The four failure identities and locations were:
  - `ranking: earlier selected filter receives priority bonus`
    (`Tests/search_test.lua:234`);
  - `ranking: full and partial matches remain in results`
    (`Tests/search_test.lua:210`);
  - `ranking: mixed stat kinds evaluate together`
    (`Tests/search_test.lua:292`); and
  - `ranking: raw score breaks an exact weighted-score tie`
    (`Tests/search_test.lua:249`).
- Targeting with `-v "Test_attributes_test.test attributes: physical above
  race median"` ran exactly one test with one success and exit code 0.
- With `LUAUNIT_SMOKE_FORCE_FAILURE=1`, targeting
  `Test_luaunit_setup_test.test_opt_in_failure_path` ran exactly one test,
  reported the intentional failure, made LuaUnit return 1, and made the direct
  child runner return 1.
- Independent sentinel probes set pre-existing `LUA_PATH` and `LUA_TEST_FILES`
  values, then ran the targeted success and forced-failure paths. Both probes
  reported `lua_path_restored=True` and `test_files_restored=True`; the failure
  probe caught `LuaUnit tests failed with exit code 1.` only after restoration.
- Static discovery used the runner's `(^test_.*|.*_test)\.lua$` convention and
  produced this sorted 57-file manifest:

