  `add_test()` bridge, and the final suite-table return.
☐ Register the file as a named `describe()` block and every existing case as a
  native `it()` block.
☐ Convert assertions according to the assertion conversion contract.
☐ Preserve dynamic case generation, names, fixture inputs, execution order
  assumptions, and support-harness isolation.
☐ Run the converted spec directly while editing it.
☐ Run the aggregate dual-framework gate after the complete batch.
☐ Record converted/residual suite counts, 332 total tests, and the exact four
  accepted failures.

Exit gate: the setup spec plus all 18 named suites run natively under Busted;
the residual LuaUnit suites and aggregate behavioral baseline remain intact.

